/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Johnson.ElongatedSquareCupola.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 63`, `matAt x 54` and `(x 72, x 73)` are a weak fit of `Johnson.ElongatedSquareCupola.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem johnsonElongatedSquareCupola_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Johnson.ElongatedSquareCupola.polyhedron Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.S N 63 54 72 := by
  rw [Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.len_eq Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.par_ok Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.zs_eq Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.weak_ok Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.poly_eq Pose.JohnsonElongatedSquareCupola.ok

